<h2>What stays the same everywhere we work</h2>
<p>Wherever your property is located, the process is the same: a Free Claim Review, a written contract with fees disclosed before any work begins, a thorough inspection, careful documentation, and ongoing communication with your insurer. Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement, and you may rescind the contract within 72 hours of signing.</p>
<p>Hidalgo County also shares a few insurance realities. It is outside the Texas Windstorm Insurance Association (TWIA) area, so wind and hail coverage typically comes from your regular insurer. Many policies carry separate wind/hail deductibles, so check your declarations page. And standard policies generally exclude flood, which matters during tropical systems such as Hurricane Dolly in 2008 and Hurricane Hanna in 2020. Our <a href="/services/storm-damage-claims/">storm damage claims</a> page explains more.</p>
